The group event publishing flow could appear to accept a newly entered event while failing to persist it when the user clicked Publish Events directly from the input form.

The root issue was that publishing only considered events already added to the queued-events list. A valid draft still present in the active input fields was excluded from the bulk payload, so the publish action could complete without creating the event the user had just typed.

The fix should treat a non-empty active draft as publishable input, build the same normalized bulk event payload for queued events and active drafts, and keep the publish button enabled whenever there is either a queued event or a valid draft for at least one selected day.
